1
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:06,712
That bell rings when the engine
buys back a token and burns it.

2
00:00:07,558 --> 00:00:11,180
On most launchpads, creator
fees land in a wallet.

3
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:12,525
And disappear.

4
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:17,762
Bellwether gives every fee a
job, and every job a receipt.

5
00:00:18,508 --> 00:00:23,912
Launch on Pons or LaunchHood, with
Bellwether as the fee recipient.

6
00:00:24,795 --> 00:00:27,305
Every claim is split exactly.

7
00:00:27,345 --> 00:00:29,630
60% to a trading book.

8
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:31,455
25% to burn your token.

9
00:00:31,495 --> 00:00:35,525
And 15% is reserved for buying
back and burning $BELL.

10
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:39,218
The book trades stock
perps on Hyperliquid,

11
00:00:39,258 --> 00:00:41,438
and profit goes back into the burn.

12
00:00:42,208 --> 00:00:46,300
Every step lands in an append-only
ledger, with a receipt.

13
00:00:46,708 --> 00:00:49,580
A reconciler checks it
against the wallets.

14
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:51,125
The books balance.

15
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:56,605
It's tested end to end against
Robinhood Chain mainnet, on a fork.

16
00:00:56,645 --> 00:00:59,162
110 checks, all passing.

17
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:03,675
Bellwether. Every fee rings the bell.
